# Evidence files are byte-exact products: the writer census classifies them by
# their on-disk dialect (utf-8, no BOM, bare LF), so git must never convert
# their line endings. Born at R2530 after core.autocrlf=true rewrote two
# repaired evidence logs towards CRLF on the next touch.
qa/*.log -text

# Queue files are written with bare LF by their per-round writers and their
# readers report lf_only, so core.autocrlf=true must not reintroduce CRLF on
# checkout. Born at R2548: the seed writer read lf_only=False straight after a
# git checkout of the same file, which is churn no reader can distinguish from
# a real edit.
state/queue/*.md text eol=lf

# The suite matrix is machine-regenerated every window by suite_matrix.py, which
# writes bare LF. Without a pin a checkout hands it back as CRLF, so the next
# --check compares CRLF on disk against regenerated LF and reports a mismatch
# that is pure dialect. Pinned to LF so a diff shows content only. CORRECTION:
# an earlier version of this comment claimed a 491/491 R2548 diff was that
# dialect churn - it was not, it was 491 genuine per-suite timing cells.
docs/sandbox-suite-matrix.md text eol=lf